==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|en|usta}} {{qualifier|colloquial}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/juːs(t).tu/|/juːs(t).tə/|lang=en}}<!--note: the final "u" deliberately has no ː/: symbol after it in IPA and SAMPA-->
* {{audio|en-us-used_to.ogg|Audio (US)|lang=en}}
* {{homophones|use to|lang=en}}
* Not homophonous with ''used'' in the sense of "made use of" (as in "the key was used to open the door"), which is {{IPA|/juːzd/|lang=en}}

===Etymology 1===
From {{m|en|used|}}, past participle of {{m|en|use||to perform habitually}} + {{m|en|to}}.

====Adjective====
{{en-adj|-}}

# {{lb|en|idiomatic|with noun phrase}} [[accustomed|Accustomed]] to, tolerant or accepting of.
#: {{ux|en|I am '''used to''' cleaning up other people’s mess.&emsp; I&nbsp;became '''used to''' his ways.}}
#* {{quote-book|year=1913|author={{w|Joseph C. Lincoln}}|chapter=5
|title=[http://openlibrary.org/works/OL5535161W Mr. Pratt's Patients]
|passage=“Well,” I says, “I cal'late a body could get '''used to''' Tophet if he stayed there long enough.” ¶ She flared up; the least mite of a slam at Doctor Wool was enough to set her going.}}
#* '''1922''', {{w|Margery Williams}}, ''{{w|The Velveteen Rabbit}}''
#*: He was shivering a little, for he had always been '''used to''' sleeping in a proper bed, and by this time his coat had worn so thin and threadbare from hugging that it was no longer any protection to him.

